-- Step 35: bank statements imported from the bank's file, and reconciling them with the books.
-- track: C
--
-- The CREATE TABLE / index statements are generated by drizzle-kit from
-- src/modules/bank-reconciliation/schema.ts. The sections marked "hand-written" are not managed
-- by Drizzle. Reverse with the file of the same name in drizzle/down.
--
-- A statement's lines are what the bank says came into or went out of one of the company's bank
-- accounts. A match ties statement lines to journal lines on that account that add up to the same
-- money; what is left unmatched on either side is what the reconciliation explains (a cheque not
-- yet presented, a bank charge not yet in the books). Nothing here posts to the books.
--
-- Database error codes of this track are SE300 to SE399 (docs/PARALLEL.md):
--   SE360  not one of the company's bank accounts in use
--   SE361  a statement's lines are not as the import reads them
--   SE362  every line of the file was imported before
--   SE363  the lines chosen to match are not this account's, or not chosen once each
--   SE364  a line is matched already
--   SE365  the lines chosen do not add up to the same money
--   SE366  no such statement or match in this company
--   SE367  a statement with matched lines is not removed

